title SM-06 User Account Lifecycle

state ACTIVE : is_active = true, deleted_at empty
state DEACTIVATED : is_active = false, deleted_at empty
state DELETED : is_active = false, deleted_at set (soft delete)

[*] --> ACTIVE : Administrator creates staff account\n[role FACILITY_MANAGER, GUARD or NORMAL_USER,\nnever ADMIN] / credentials e-mailed after commit
[*] --> ACTIVE : Administrator imports accounts from file\n[valid row with face photo] / import_batch_id set,\nface data registered, credentials e-mailed

ACTIVE --> DEACTIVATED : Administrator deactivates [not own account]\n/ open requests cancelled (SYSTEM), AP revoked,\nWebSocket sessions closed, AI face cache refreshed
DEACTIVATED --> ACTIVE : Administrator reactivates\n/ nothing restored automatically

ACTIVE --> DELETED : Administrator deletes account [not own account]\nor removes its import batch\n/ same side effects as deactivation
DEACTIVATED --> DELETED : Administrator deletes account [not own account]\nor removes its import batch

DELETED --> ACTIVE : Administrator restores import batch\n[user code and e-mail not used by a live account]\n/ skipped accounts reported

note right of DEACTIVATED
  DEACTIVATED and DELETED accounts cannot log in
  (password, Google or reset link) and existing JWTs
  are refused by JwtAuthenticationFilter.
  Guest visits hosted by the account keep their status;
  guest entry is denied at decision time (HOST_LOST_ACCESS).
end note

note left of DELETED
  No single-account restore.
  Only imported accounts (import_batch_id set)
  can return, and they always return as ACTIVE.
end note
@enduml
